# Task 18 — Mafia stub chunk (Phase 3, 5h)

Rfc anchors: §14.1, A13, M3.2. Proves the chunk protocol end-to-end with a
real consumer package.

> **Two-repo note (v2.2):** this task spans `telegram-game-mafia` (own
> git repo, own plan: `docs/tasks/mafia/todo.mafia.md`) and the host/menu side
> (hub test rig). Sequence explicitly: (1) mafia-repo PR ships build setup +
> stub + webApi handler behind its own suite; (2) host-side PR wires the rig +
> E2E. A single cross-repo "PR" is impossible — record both PR links in this
> task's acceptance evidence; coordinate with the mafia plan so the stub does
> not collide with its game-logic milestones.
>
> **Implementation note (2026-08-30):** executed as a single workspace change
> set across both repos (user reviews/commits per repo). Both sides of the
> evidence below landed together.

## Goal

A minimal but honest game screen in `telegram-game-mafia` that mounts
through the loader, uses every bridge capability, and degrades correctly.

## Read first

- Task 17's loader (installed behavior), §18 chunk skeleton, §14.1 features
   vocabulary; mafia repo conventions (`docs/tasks/mafia/todo.mafia.md`
   context, module layout rules from AGENTS.md).

## Deliverables

1. Build setup in the mafia module producing a content-hashed chunk bundle
   (`app.<hash>.js`), publish tag `<module>-assets`, manifest updated to
   `UiEntry::Chunk(url)` + declared `features: ['context','navigation',
   'resources','haptics','fullscreen']`.
2. Stub game screen: renders themed board placeholder from theme(); uses
   bridge.fetch against a stub mafia webApi route (`POST 'session/join'`,
   minRole member, chatScope Required); one `bridge.searchResources('chat')`
   call rendering the result as a plain list (proves the D41 resources path
   end-to-end); requests fullscreen via the granted `'fullscreen'` surface +
   landscape orientation lock (degrades to text when the feature is absent);
   back handler ownership demo (exits fullscreen first if active);
   haptic on actions; graceful text when any granted feature is missing
   (degraded in-chunk copy, not crash).
3. WebApi handler in mafia module implementing routes()/handle() with
   TgUiContext usage only (no session/DB identity reads — G9 exemplar).
4. E2E/browser test wiring: mount through real loader in the hub test rig;
   A13 checklist executed and archived (credentials isolation, navigation via
   bridge only, degraded path by forcing feature removal).

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] A13 passes as written in §21.3.
- [x] Doctor (task 22 smoke mode acceptable) reports no chunk findings:
      asset present, hash-name consistent, protocol id ok — asserted
      mechanically by `tests/browser/mafia-chunk.e2e.test.ts` (single hashed
      bundle, handshake id/api/features) and the
      `exposes a content-hashed chunk url` Pest case.
- [x] Chunk size within NFR-5 soft budget: 2.97 kB (1.28 kB gzip) — no
      warning possible.

## Evidence (2026-08-30)

- Mafia repo: `vite.mafia-chunk.config.mjs` + `tools/build-chunk.mjs`
  (`npm run build`, vite resolved from the host node_modules — same
  convention as the menu module) → `public/vendor/menu-modules/mafia/app.<hash>.js`
  + `resources/chunk/build-manifest.json`; publish tag `mafia-assets`
  (`MafiaServiceProvider::boot`). `MafiaUi` (chunk manifest, UiKind::Game)
  and `MafiaUiHandler` (POST session/join, Member, ChatScope::Required,
  TgUiContext-only — G9 exemplar) registered via
  `MafiaModule::register()` (+ capability `Ui`, `requiresModules: menu`).
  Stub screen `resources/chunk/main.ts`: themed board, bridge.fetch join,
  searchResources('chat') list, fullscreen toggle + landscape degrade,
  exclusive back handler (fullscreen first), haptics, per-feature degraded
  copy. Mafia suite: 104 passed / 1002 assertions.
- §14.1 v2.4 seam fix (host side, documented in menu.md §14.1): the chunk
  cannot author the bridge — `chunkLoader.loadChunk` now takes
  `ChunkLoaderDeps {mountEl, createBridge}` and `ready()` RETURNS the frozen
  host bridge; `ChunkRuntime` mounts into the always-rendered viewport and
  `bridge-mock.ts` mirrors the contract. `App.tsx` passes the full host
  feature vocabulary (the loader intersects with the chunk handshake).
- Host E2E: `tests/browser/mafia-chunk.e2e.test.ts` (real loader × real
  bundle: handshake, frozen bridge, fetch/resources/haptics, degraded paths,
  unknown-token rejection) and `tests/Feature/MafiaChunkE2ETest.php` (real
  MafiaUi/MafiaUiHandler through the real dispatcher: chat-scope 403, join
  200, module_disabled 404, hashed-asset presence).

## Verification

```
# mafia repo (its own npm setup, per the two-repo note):
cd misc/BAGArt/telegram-bot-mafia-module && npm run build
# host side:
php artisan test --compact --filter='Mafia|ChunkE2E'
```

## Guardrails

The stub must not grow into game logic — that lives in the mafia module's own
plan; this task proves transport only.

## Engine alignment notes

- **Module enablement gates chunk availability:** the mafia module's
  `UiEntry::Chunk(url)` manifest is only served by the hub when the module is
  enabled via `ModuleActivationService` (engine). The hub's assembler (task 09)
  checks activation state before including the module's `UiEntry` in the
  bootstrap response. A disabled module never yields a chunk entry.
- **Dependency chain validation:** the engine's `EffectiveDependencyResolver`
  verifies that mafia's `requiresModules` dependencies are satisfied before
  activation. If dependencies are unmet, the chunk entry is absent from the
  bootstrap — the hub never attempts to load a chunk for a module whose
  prerequisites are missing.
- **Engine does NOT load chunks:** chunk loading (script injection, lifecycle)
  is entirely hub-side (task 17). The engine's role is limited to activation
  gating; it never touches `<script>` elements or the `TgMenuBridge`.
